      "assistant_text": "The [[write-journal]] page describes how the guarded write path journals file state before making changes. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n**Core function**: The system records each file\u0027s prior state (its previous content, or the fact that it didn\u0027t exist) in an in-memory write journal *before* overwriting it.\n\n**Rollback capability**: If the agent run fails\u2014whether due to a turn cap being exceeded, an unrecoverable error, or write denials\u2014the journal can roll back all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring original content for files that existed before, and deleting newly created files.\n\n**Transaction semantics**: This provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without needing a database transaction\u2014the in-memory journal itself acts as a transaction log for the duration of a single run.\n\n**Query agent exception**: The Query agent (which this system prompt describes) never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool at all; the journal mechanism exists in the shared runtime library but is only used by agents that actually write files.",
